<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhang Qian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 113 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhang Qian was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> envoy sent west by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-han">Emperor Wu</a> around 138 BCE to seek an alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuezhi">Yuezhi</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a>. Held captive by the Xiongnu for years, he reached Dayuan, Kangju and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a> and returned in 126 BCE; a later mission went to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wusun">Wusun</a>. His reports gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> its first detailed knowledge of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and opened the way for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zhang-qian.jpg" alt="Zhang Qian" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PHG · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ZhangQianTravels.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
